  "question": {
    "text": "A solution of $\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}$ and $\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ has $\\mathrm{pH}=8.0 .$ Which of the following hydroxides may be precipitated when this solution is mixed with equal volume of 0.2 M of metal ion."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Ba}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=1.1 \\times 10^{-4}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=3.5 \\times 10^{-4}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=8.1 \\times 10^{-16}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=2.1 \\times 10^{-5}\\right)$ ).",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{pH}=8, \\mathrm{pOH}=6 ;\\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]=10^{-6} \\mathrm{M}$\r\n\r\nIonic product of $\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}=0.2 \\times\\left(1 \\times 10^{-6}\\right)^{2}$\r\n\r\n$=2 \\times 10^{-13}>\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\left(=8.1 \\times 10^{-16}\\right)$"
  }
